<title>AUSTRALIA: CBA cuts Australian fixed home loan rates.</title>
<headline>CBA cuts Australian fixed home loan rates.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commonwealth Bank of Australia (CBA) said on Tuesday it would cut its fixed home loan interest rates by up to half a percentage point.</p>
<p>New rates are two years 7.20 percent (previously 7.50); three years 7.65 percent (7.90 percent); four years 7.90 percent (8.20 percent) and five years 7.95 percent (8.45 percent). The one year guaranteed rate is unchanged at 6.99 percent.</p>
<p>The bank said its two and five-year fixed rates were the lowest among all Australian home loan providers.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
